 "reading": "Before costs the bracket has a small positive drift (T1 +0.050R a trade out of sample, month t +1.50; +0.084R in sample), but with a median risk of $13.76 the $0.60 round trip and the buys' financing take 0.061R a trade and leave −0.011R (t −0.32); at 2x costs −0.071R. The gross drift is the buys (out of sample +0.098R gross, +0.027R net, n 595) while the sells make −0.002R gross: the same pattern as gold's rise over 2017-26, not a property of the inside bar. T1 beat 34 of 40 same-side random trades of equal size and hold (baseline −0.042R), short of the 38 needed. T2 (no target) and T3 (buy stop only) fail too: T3 −0.018R out of sample against a random-buy baseline of −0.003R (beaten by 14 of 40) and −0.059R in sample; T2 −0.015R. Like the daily inside day (`gold-inside-day`), the H4 inside bar is not an edge on gold after costs; no follow-up is proposed.",
